From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephen Bates <stephen.bates@amd.com>
Date: 2026-08-04
Subject: [PATCH 12] feat: add Prometheus prefetch hit counters (L1/L2)

LMCache's Prometheus endpoint at :8080/metrics only exposed memory-usage
gauges.  This patch adds four Prometheus metrics:

  lmcache_mp_prefetch_hit_chunks_total{tier="l1"}  -- DRAM L1 hits
  lmcache_mp_prefetch_hit_chunks_total{tier="l2"}  -- NVMe L2 hits
  lmcache_mp_prefetch_miss_chunks_total             -- chunks not found
  lmcache_mp_prefetch_requests_total                -- completed lookups

Uses register_observable_counter (OTel observable counter via callback),
not a synchronous Counter, because lmcache's /metrics endpoint calls
generate_latest(REGISTRY) directly.  Synchronous OTel Counters register
with a separate OTel Prometheus registry invisible to that call.  Observable
instruments register via callbacks with the default REGISTRY correctly.

Counters are pre-seeded with 0.001 so they appear in Prometheus from the
first scrape before any prefetch completes.  Seeding with exactly 0 causes
OTel Prometheus exporter v1.40.0 to suppress the observation.

Grafana chunk hit-rate formula (bounded [0,1]):
  rate(lmcache_mp_prefetch_hit_chunks_total[1m])
  / (  rate(lmcache_mp_prefetch_hit_chunks_total[1m])
     + rate(lmcache_mp_prefetch_miss_chunks_total[1m]))

Note: lmcache_mp_prefetch_requests_total counts lookup calls, not chunks.
Dividing hit_chunks/s by requests/s yields average hit chunks per request
which is unbounded and not a hit rate.  Use hits/(hits+misses) for a [0,1]
chunk-level cache hit rate.

Applies after patches 01-11.
